From 16867e61c541665ddbd31a1b2c7dfcaf00702451 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:14:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): hold the pinned-checkout verdict through
 recovery, the manual sweep and migration [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review of the two commits before this one found paths that did not share the verdict:

- `python -m` puts the working directory ahead of PYTHONPATH unless safe-path mode is on;
  _gateway_code_root now probes in the interpreter's order and only for a plain
  `python -m …` launch (other interpreter options can change the import path), so a
  gateway started inside checkout A with PYTHONPATH naming B is read as A.
- the manual-process sweep stopped a pinned unit's gateway whenever its unit PID lookup
  failed; it now drops gateways on another checkout first.
- restart-abort recovery restarted every planned profile it had not seen restarted; its
  partition now reads each profile's live gateway itself (it can run before the restart
  phase looked at any unit) and lists a pinned one as skipped with the reason.
- the post-update multiplex migration could fold (stop and uninstall) a pinned unit that is
  not `gateway.standalone`; a code-root guard blocks it.
- a supervisor that cannot be disarmed (systemctl stop / launchctl bootout failing) raised a
  refusal without gateway names, so its deferrals never built a streak.
---
